[Slide 206] Best Practices for Error Handling Design
‑
Fail Fast:‑Detect‑and report errors as early as possible to simplify
debugging. Use assertions or invariant checks in development
builds.
‑
Graceful Degradation:‑Where‑possible, degrade functionality
rather than crashing entirely (e.g., read cached data if live fetch
Department‑of‑CSE‑–‑UE23CS341A
fails).
‑
Consistent Strategy:‑Apply‑uniform error-handling conventions
(return vs. exception) across the codebase to minimize cognitive
load.
‑
Automated Tests:‑Include‑negative test cases for error paths,
ensuring errors are raised and handled as expected.
